  "notes": "World = arm base frame (so101.xml). The table / tent floor is NOT at z = 0: fitted plane z = c0 + c1 x + c2 y (scene.table_plane; -4.7 mm at the base, about -16 mm at x = 0.3 m; tilt 2.1 deg down along +x, 1.1 deg up along +y). The black mat lies on it (rectangle 0.308 x 0.460 m, centre (0.273, -0.004), yaw -3.9 deg). Tent floor (white) edges on the table plane: table edge behind the robot at x ~ -0.04 (the base is clamped there, nothing beyond it), back wall bottom at y ~ +0.46, front edge at y ~ -0.45, right wall bottom at x ~ 0.59 (tent_edges_on_table); walls white, an LED strip along the top of the far (+x) side, the room (dark, a yellow wall) visible beyond the open table edge. All tent / mat edges are rotated by about -3.5 deg about z relative to the base axes (either the base is turned on the table or the pan zero is off by that much). Cube 30 mm (resting centre 15 mm above the local table), plate 50 x 50 mm, thickness held at 2 mm (prior; not resolved by the data). The real wrist camera is NOT at the MJCF wrist_cam pose: fitted pose in camera_mount is ~4.7 cm further back along the gripper axis and ~1.7 cm further out than the MJCF camera (the external view shows the camera board on a taller bracket). Image time lags the joint state by time_offset_frames (about 1.3-1.4 frames = 42-48 ms) in both cameras."
